  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b1a7c0de-f1a9-4b2c-9d3e-flagbasecol02",
    "name": "FlagBase API",
    "description": "FlagBase dashboard API (`apps/dashboard`) — full RESTful surface.\n\n**Auth is cookie-based.** Sign Up / Sign In set an httpOnly `flagbase_session` cookie; Postman's cookie jar stores and re-sends it, so there is no bearer token to copy.\n\n**Nested, org-scoped URLs.** Projects and flags live under an organization: `…/organizations/{orgId}/projects/{projectId}/flags/{flagId}`. IDs are captured into collection variables as you go (`orgId`, `projectId`, `flagId`, `memberId`, `invitationId`).\n\n**Before running:**\n1. `pnpm dashboard:dev` (http://localhost:3000).\n2. Mongo replica set reachable + `apps/dashboard/.env.local` (`MONGODB_URI`, `SESSION_SECRET`). Without them the API routes return 500.\n\n**Runner order** is arranged so a full top-to-bottom pass works: create → read → update flows for every resource, with the destructive deletes gathered in **Teardown** at the end. Two folders need a second actor and stay green via lenient checks: **Members → Change Role/Remove** target the sole owner (a policy error is expected), and **Invitation Actions** need a real token from the invite email/console log.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
